From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:59:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: CPU cores only as far as the system reports them

Repository: https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch
Base: fastfetch 2.70.0, 17bb3fd2384bd814b421d73b8c8b8d08e06cfa26
Problem: the CPU backend wrote processor.resource's processor count as
physical, logical and online cores alike and set the package count to 1.
Those are different facts: the count is of logical processors the kernel
found, and a uniprocessor exec runs tasks on one of them only. On a
two-processor QEMU guest with a uniprocessor exec the JSON said
"online": 2.
Solution: the count is the logical processors. Online is that count when
exec is an SMP build (it alone provides execlock.resource; the system's
own code tests SMP that way), else 1. Physical cores and packages are not
reported on AROS and stay 0 (JSON: physical 0, packages null).
Scope: detection/cpu/cpu_aros.c.
Upstream-Status: AROS only; part of the AROS backend.
Verification: cross-built for the three targets. Guest runs:
docs/evidence/2026-10-27-r2/.
Removal: with the AROS backend.
---
 src/detection/cpu/cpu_aros.c | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/detection/cpu/cpu_aros.c b/src/detection/cpu/cpu_aros.c
index 4afeeb5..ca6e75c 100644
--- a/src/detection/cpu/cpu_aros.c
+++ b/src/detection/cpu/cpu_aros.c
@@ -23,10 +23,17 @@ const char* ffDetectCPUImpl([[maybe_unused]] const FFCPUOptions* options, FFCPUR
         return "processor.resource does not name this processor";
     }
     ffArosStrbufSetNative(&cpu->name, (const char*) model);
-    // Processors the system found; whether exec schedules on all of them
-    // (an SMP build) is not reported here.
-    cpu->coresPhysical = cpu->coresLogical = cpu->coresOnline = (uint16_t) count;
-    cpu->packages = count ? 1 : 0;
+    // processor.resource counts the logical processors the kernel found
+    // (on PC, the APICs). Only an SMP exec runs tasks on more than the boot
+    // processor; it, and nothing else, provides execlock.resource (system
+    // code tests SMP the same way). Cores per package and the package count
+    // are not reported on AROS: they stay 0, unknown.
+    cpu->coresLogical = (uint16_t) count;
+    if (count) {
+        cpu->coresOnline = OpenResource((CONST_STRPTR) "execlock.resource") ? (uint16_t) count : 1;
+    }
+    cpu->coresPhysical = 0;
+    cpu->packages = 0;
     if (speed) {
         cpu->frequencyBase = (uint32_t) (speed / 1000000);
     }
